     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **850 mg twice daily with meals:** 1,700 mg/day. This may be what you meant if 1,700 mg was the daily total.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg three times daily with meals**, or another dose.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm that. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
